{"name":"Skyway","hex":"#a6bbcf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Skyway","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of Metro Manila Skyway."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Skyway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skyway","blocks":[{"text":"A skyway, skybridge, skywalk or sky walkway is an elevated pedestrian walkway connecting two or more buildings in an urban area, or connecting elevated points within mountainous recreational zones. Urban skyways very often take the form of enclosed or covered footbridges that protect pedestrians from the weather. Open-top modern skyways in mountains now often have glass bottoms. Sometimes enclosed urban skywalks are made almost totally from glass, including ceilings, walls and floors. Some urban skyways function strictly as linear parks designed for walking."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/2008-03-14_Spring_St_skyways_in_Atlanta.jpg/330px-2008-03-14_Spring_St_skyways_in_Atlanta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyway"},{"title":"Skyway (Disney)","blocks":[{"text":"The Skyway was a gondola lift attraction at Disneyland, at the Magic Kingdom, and at Tokyo Disneyland. Since all versions of this attraction took riders back and forth between Fantasyland and Tomorrowland, the route from Tomorrowland was called Skyway to Fantasyland, and the route from Fantasyland was called Skyway to Tomorrowland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Matterhorn_Skyway_straight_on.jpg/330px-Matterhorn_Skyway_straight_on.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyway_(Disney)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Pottery_tower_6.JPG/500px-Pottery_tower_6.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Pottery_tower_6.JPG/1280px-Pottery_tower_6.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Pottery_tower_6.JPG/500px-Pottery_tower_6.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Han dynasty (202 BC – 220 AD) Chinese miniature model of two residential towers joined by a skyway","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APottery_tower_6.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Antonio_Contin_-_Ponte_dei_sospiri_%28Venice%29.jpg/500px-Antonio_Contin_-_Ponte_dei_sospiri_%28Venice%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Antonio_Contin_-_Ponte_dei_sospiri_%28Venice%29.jpg/1280px-Antonio_Contin_-_Ponte_dei_sospiri_%28Venice%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Antonio_Contin_-_Ponte_dei_sospiri_%28Venice%29.jpg/500px-Antonio_Contin_-_Ponte_dei_sospiri_%28Venice%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Bridge of Sighs in Venice, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntonio_Contin_-_Ponte_dei_sospiri_(Venice).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/It%C3%A4v%C3%A4yl%C3%A4_kuvattuna_it%C3%A4keskuksen_kohdalta.JPG/500px-It%C3%A4v%C3%A4yl%C3%A4_kuvattuna_it%C3%A4keskuksen_kohdalta.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/It%C3%A4v%C3%A4yl%C3%A4_kuvattuna_it%C3%A4keskuksen_kohdalta.JPG/1280px-It%C3%A4v%C3%A4yl%C3%A4_kuvattuna_it%C3%A4keskuksen_kohdalta.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/